<title>FRANCE: US top country of origin for Paris Jan-Oct imports.</title>
<headline>US top country of origin for Paris Jan-Oct imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at Paris airports in January-October 1996 , Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The principal countries of origin for ADP imports during the period January-October 1996, with percentage change on January-October 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	   124,851 tonnes  up    3.0pct</p>
<p> 2  India			25,021 tonnes  up   28.0</p>
<p> 3  Canada		     21,802 tonnes  up    1.5</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong		  16,538 tonnes  down  4.6</p>
<p> 5  Japan			16,073 tonnes  down 11.6</p>
<p> 6  United Kingdom	   14,272 tonnes  down  9.1</p>
<p> 7  Germany		    12,598 tonnes  up    0.2</p>
<p> 8  Italy			10,413 tonnes  up    0.9</p>
<p> 9  Thailand		    9,232 tonnes  down 19.0</p>
<p> 10 Kenya			 8,699 tonnes  down  7.8</p>
<p> 11 French West Indies	6,884 tonnes  down  3.0</p>
<p> 12 Senegal		     6,229 tonnes  up   40.0</p>
<p> 13 United Arab Emirates    6,006 tonnes  down  6.8</p>
<p> 14 Morocco		     5,624 tonnes  down  5.6</p>
<p> 15 Argentina		   5,189 tonnes  up   18.8</p>
<p> 16 South Africa		5,001 tonnes  up   13.7</p>
<p> 17 China			 4,440 tonnes  up    5.2</p>
<p> 18 Israel			4,256 tonnes  dwon 14.3</p>
<p> 19 Mexico			4,183 tonnes  down  3.3</p>
<p> 20 Singapore		   4,174 tonnes  down  7.2</p>
<p> Total			  311,485 tonnes</p>
<p>Global January-October 1996 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 428,521 tonnes, an increase of 1.1 percent on the same period last year, ADP said.</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
